-- title:
--   Membership in a translated set
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a normed additive group, $S \subseteq E$ a subset and $x \in E$. Write $S + x$ (`shift S x`) for the translate of $S$ by $x$. Then for every $y \in E$,
--   $$y \in S + x \iff y - x \in S .$$
--
--   This is the defining property of translation, recorded as a rewriting rule so that statements about translated sets — most importantly about cones $V[x]$ translated to be based at a point $x$ — reduce mechanically to statements about the untranslated set applied to the difference vector. Since the whole cone formalism is stated for differences of points, this is the lemma that connects the two points of view.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The statement is a `simp` lemma, so it is applied automatically during simplification. It needs only the additive normed group structure — no inner product, no completeness, and no hypothesis on $S$ (which need not be measurable, closed or nonempty).
